# The volume's top, handed to storage's own user (1000, see `app`), which makes
# what it keeps under it itself. Not recursive: everything below is that user's
# already, made by it, and a walk of the whole volume at every boot would cost
# in proportion to what it holds.
type = scripted
command = /bin/busybox chown 1000:1000 /data
depends-on: data
